<header class="sg-head"><p class="featured-region">Anthem · 1847 · Sub-Saharan Africa</p><h1 class="sg-title">All Hail, Liberia, Hail!</h1><p class="sg-kid" data-say>The national anthem of Liberia, the official anthem since the country became independent in 1847.</p></header>
<dl class="sg-facts"><div><dt>Words</dt><dd>Daniel Bashiel Warner</dd></div><div><dt>Music</dt><dd>Olmstead Luca</dd></div><div><dt>Culture</dt><dd>The Republic of Liberia</dd></div><div><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd></div><div><dt>Place</dt><dd>Liberia</dd></div><div><dt>Date</dt><dd>national anthem from independence in 1847</dd></div><div><dt>Type</dt><dd>Anthem</dd></div><div><dt>The words</dt><dd>Public domain (words by Daniel Bashiel Warner (he died in 1880), music by Olmstead Luca (he died in 1869))</dd></div></dl>
<div class="sg-body">
<section class="sg-sec" id="story"><h2>The story</h2><p>&quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/all-hail-liberia-hail">All Hail, Liberia, Hail!</a>&quot; is the national anthem of Liberia. Its words were written by Daniel Bashiel Warner (1815–1880), who later became the third president of Liberia, and its music was composed by Olmstead Luca (1826–1869). It became the official national anthem when Liberia became independent in 1847.</p><p>In the 1970s the anthem was reconsidered along with the country's other national symbols. On 22 July 1974 the Legislature of Liberia passed an act allowing the president to set up a commission to consider changes to a number of national symbols, among them the anthem and the flag. President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-tolbert">William Tolbert</a> appointed 51 members to the Commission on National Unity, headed by McKinley Alfred Deshield Sr. and also called the Deshield Commission, which set out to re-examine the symbols and remove what divided Liberians. Its report, submitted on 24 January 1978, recommended changing one word of the anthem. The change was never made, and the anthem is sung with its original words.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="meaning"><h2>What it says</h2><p>A patriotic hymn that hails Liberia as a free nation and calls its people to unity and loyalty. The mood is proud and solemn.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="words"><h2>The words</h2><div class="sg-blocks"><div class="sg-lyrics sg-cols-1"><div class="sg-colhead" aria-hidden="true"><span class="sg-o">The words</span></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>All hail, Liberia, hail! (All hail!)</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>This glorious land of liberty</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>Shall long be ours.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>Though new her name,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>Grand be her fame,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>And mighty be her powers,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>And mighty be her powers,</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>In joy and gladness</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>With our hearts united,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>We'll shout the freedom</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>Of a race benighted,</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>Long live Liberia, happy land!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>A home of glorious liberty,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>By God's command!</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>All hail, Liberia, hail! (All hail!)</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>In union strong success is sure</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>We cannot fail!</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>With God above</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>Our rights to prove</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>We will o'er all prevail,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>We will o'er all prevail,</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>With heart and hand</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>Our country's cause defending</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>We'll meet the foe</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>With valor unpretending.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>Long live Liberia, happy land!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>A home of glorious liberty,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" data-say>By God's command!</span></p></div></div></div><div class="sg-credit"><p>Words: Daniel Bashiel Warner; as quoted in Wikipedia's article. Text from <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/All_Hail%2C_Liberia%2C_Hail!" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikipedia</a>; public domain.</p></div></section>
</div>
